<p>
  Holds the answer to the usage-metrics question. It is created disabled on first boot, which means declined.
</p>

<p>
  <strong>What it affects.</strong> Two things read this capability:
</p>

<ul>
  <li>The consent banner in the footer appears only while no capability of this type exists. Because one is created
    at startup, the banner never appears.</li>
  <li>Maven proxy repositories append a marker to their outbound <code>User-Agent</code> saying which answer was
    given: <code>pad</code> when declined, <code>pae</code> when enabled, <code>pau</code> when unanswered. Upstream
    repositories such as Maven Central see this marker on every request.</li>
</ul>

<p>
  <strong>What it does not do.</strong> This edition ships no code that collects or transmits usage metrics. Enabling
  the capability records consent and changes the User-Agent marker; it starts no reporting, because there is nothing
  here to report with.
</p>

<p>
  <strong>Changing the answer.</strong> Enable this capability to opt in, disable it to decline. Deleting it returns
  the instance to the unanswered state, which brings the banner back on the next page load.
</p>
